  {
   "id": 1096688,
   "title": "Pro tip: inserting the nuts",
   "updated": "2026-07-14 14:10:34",
   "lines": [
    {
     "html": "3D printed parts are very precise, however, there still might be a tolerance in the printed part and the same goes for the size of the nut.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Therefore it might happen, that the nut won't fit easily in or might be falling out. Let's see, how to fix it:",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Nut won't fit in</strong>: use a screw with a thread along its entire length (typically: M3x10, M3x18) and screw it from the opposite side of the opening. While tightening the screw, the nut will be pulled in. Remove the screw afterwards.",
     "color": "green",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Nut keeps falling out</strong>: Use a piece of tape to fix the nut temporarily in place, as soon as you insert the screw in, you can remove the tape. <em>Using glue isn't recommended as it can partly reach into the thread and you won't be able to tighten the screw properly.</em>",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "Every time we recommend using the \"screw pulling technique\", you will be reminded with Joe's avatar ;)",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Parts in the pictures are used as an example.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": "note",
     "level": 0
    }
   ],
   "gallery": [
    {
     "original": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/73236842de53d300f04b78c6965d2e17.jpg",
