  {
   "id": 1096748,
   "title": "Electronics protection (ESD)",
   "updated": "2026-07-14 14:10:38",
   "lines": [
    {
     "html": "<strong>WARNING</strong>: Make sure to <strong>protect the electronics against electrostatic discharge (ESD)</strong>. Always unpack the electronics right before you need them!",
     "color": null,
     "icon": "caution",
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Here are some <strong>tips to prevent damage to the electronics:</strong>",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Keep the electronics inside the ESD bag</strong> right until you are asked to install them.",
     "color": "green",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Always touch the sides of the board only</strong> while handling it. Avoid touching the components on the surface.",
     "color": "orange",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Before you touch the electronics </strong>use any conductive (metal) structure nearby to neutralize the possible static charge from your hands.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "Be extra cautious <strong>in rooms with carpets</strong>, which are often a source of electrostatic energy.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "Clothes made of wool or certain synthetic fabrics can easily gather static electricity too. It is safer to wear cotton clothing for the assembly.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    }
   ],
   "gallery": [
    {
     "original": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2d6c14b2396f2862c9384a598d1fd78f.jpg",
